WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.090
- [Narrator] Once upon a
time, there was a mighty king.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.200
It was said he ruled over a small island

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.080
off the coast of Sardinia.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.060
Many had searched far and
wide for the lost king,

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.200
but still no one had found--
(tape screeching)

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.420
Wait a minute, that's him.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.701
That's the king.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:18.318
(trumpet music)

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:22.507
(speaks in foreign language)

00:00:22.507 --> 00:00:26.174
(lively instrumental music)

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.180
- [Narrator] His family
has lived on the island

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.230
for over 200 years.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.400
His great-great-grandfather,
Giuseppe Bertoleoni,

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.920
arrived on the uninhabited island in 1807.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.330
The king of Sardinia, Carlo Alberto,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.830
was, well, intrigued, so ...

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.783
- [Narrator] Goats with gold teeth?

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.430
- [Narrator] A Bertoleoni
coat of arms were painted,

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.630
flags were made, and a
royal family tree was drawn.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.440
News had even reached Queen Victoria

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.433
who sent a photographer to
photograph the new royal family.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.300
- [Narrator] So what is
a typical day in the life

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.293
of his lordship?

00:01:56.726 --> 00:01:58.640
- [Narrator] Wait, a
ruler with a restaurant?

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.743
Are you really a king?

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:34.150
- [Narrator] Your
Majesty, I totally agree.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.900
(gentle instrumental music)

